      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-21T21:47:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "you need `get_pid_task` here because once you call `rcu_read_unlock` and later `task_unlock`, the `task` can be destroyed from under you. You need to take a refcount on it, which is what `get_pid_task` will do. It also does `rcu_read_lock/rcu_read_unlock` internally, so you won\u0027t need them here.\n\nBut don\u0027t forget `put_task_struct(task)` once you don\u0027t need it anymore.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "f5d3e6252fe28848105686d3a97420b6bc9964e1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
